      "content": "Adjusting the timing or dosage without a doctor's advice is risky and might not effectively resolve your issue. Pacing the medication throughout the day could potentially help with tolerability, but it's important to note that optimal daily dosing a physician determines. Taking lisinopril at night does not address the root problem, as it was prescribed based on your body's specific needs. A portion of your dose just at night might even increase daytime dizziness instead of reducing it. If you can't find your doctor and you experience severe dizziness or any other worrying symptoms, please consider visiting an urgent care center or emergency department as a precautionary step. Your health and safety should be the top priority.",
